Note: the current weather in Almaty from the Open-Meteo service, read straight from JSON.
Note: another address of the same service can be given: engc.py run weather.eng "https://..."

a report has a current weather (a weather).
a weather has a temperature (decimal), a windspeed (decimal) and a weathercode (number).

set address to "https://api.open-meteo.com/v1/forecast?latitude=43.25&longitude=76.95&current_weather=true".
if the number of items in the arguments is more than 0, set address to item 1 of the arguments.

try the following.
  fetch address into page.
  set report to page as a report.
  set now to the current weather of report.
  say "Almaty:" and then the temperature of now with 1 decimals and then "°C, wind"
    and then the windspeed of now with 1 decimals and then "km/h.".
  if the weathercode of now is 0, say "Clear sky.".
  otherwise say "Weather code" and then the weathercode of now and then ".".
if something goes wrong
  say "Could not get the weather:" and then the error.
that's all.
